          "Address renter economic anxiety with specificity: the 36.5% renter rate in a $104,075-income district signals housing cost pressure even among affluent professionals, and affordability constraints on younger households and fixed-income older adults. Housing policy, education costs, and healthcare affordability are not fringe concerns for this constituency — they are the material constraints on the life outcomes renters expected.",
