          "Lead with housing affordability and renter protection: with 50.8% renters and $84K median income, the district's economic foundation is unstable housing costs and tenant vulnerability; a concrete agenda on rent control, tenant rights, and affordable housing production is more consequential to this constituency than most other state-level issues.",
