          "Make housing affordability the primary governing agenda item: 41.4% renter rate in a $100,384-income district is not a normal housing market — it is a failure of zoning and development policy; any candidate who wants to consolidate the incumbent's coalition or build a viable challenge must offer concrete answers on why housing is unaffordable despite high incomes and what legislative change will unlock homeownership for the professional renter majority.",
