          "Center housing affordability and tenant protections as primary legislative priorities: the 38.6% renter rate in a $101K income district signals renters paying substantial proportions of income to housing. For a constituency that is disproportionately Asian-American immigrants and younger professionals, tenant protection, rent stabilization, housing development policy, and enforcement against discriminatory practices in housing markets are material economic concerns that deserve legislative focus proportional to their constituency impact.",
          "Engage the Asian-American community with specificity around immigration policy, educational equity, and small-business support: at 61.56% of the district, Asian-American voters are not a constituency to be addressed generically. Immigration reform, citizenship pathways, discrimination protections in education and employment, and support for immigrant small-business owners operating in California's regulatory environment are the policy issues most likely to generate sustained constituent satisfaction and legitimacy.",
