          "Engage the 42% Asian plurality with specificity on the issues that activate Asian American voters in affluent professional districts: education funding and college affordability, immigration policy and family reunification, small business regulation and tax fairness, and healthcare access including mental health services. Generic Republican or Democratic positioning will underperform among voters who evaluate individual candidates on concrete policy rather than inherited partisan loyalty.",
          "Address the renter 30% directly on housing costs and affordability: in a district where median income is $131,590 but 29.7% of households rent, the gap between regional housing costs and even high household incomes is creating material financial pressure. Young professionals, immigrant families, and service-sector workers paying market-rate rents in San Diego deserve specific housing policy solutions, not assumption that income level alone solves affordability.",
