          "Address housing affordability and cost-of-living pressures directly: at $116.5K median income with 28.7% renters and a 34.1-year median age, younger professionals and established families are evaluating on whether government is managing the cost of living or exacerbating it through regulation, zoning, and tax policy. This is the material economic issue most likely to drive electoral movement in a high-income coastal district.",
          "Engage the 14.4% Hispanic community and the 6.9% demographic gap with specific constituent attention and programming; in a district where the Asian plurality dominates the demographic narrative, other communities can become invisible to representation and to electoral turnout efforts.",
