          "Address the 16.9% college-educated population gap with specificity: trade apprenticeships, community college affordability, and pathways from secondary education to family-sustaining wages are the education-access issues for a working-class district where four in five adults lack a college degree.",
          "Treat 55% as a working margin, not a safe floor: the combination of younger median age (34.8), renter plurality (38.4%), and a rising Hispanic population signals a district where active constituent engagement and visible economic delivery are prerequisites to holding the seat, not optional enhancements."
