          "Address housing affordability for high-income homeowners: at $152.7K median income and 81.3% homeownership, the district's material concern is not low-income housing access but the relationship between professional incomes and property values, property taxes, and the cost of maintaining affluent neighborhood character; property tax policy and development regulations are the concrete issues that shape homeowner quality of life.",
